190
00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:22.955
The meeting includes a few people.

191
00:10:22.955 --> 00:10:25.958
There's a date associated with the meeting
and so on.

192
00:10:26.092 --> 00:10:31.092
Again, let's run this pipeline with
this text as input to our prompt builder.

193
00:10:31.564 --> 00:10:36.564
And when we're happy with the responses,
let's print it out in green.

194
00:10:36.569 --> 00:10:41.040
Again, we notice that the first time
the NLM created entities,

195
00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:44.310
it had person dates,
but it also had technology.

196
00:10:44.343 --> 00:10:48.648
Technology was not one of the entities
we asked for it to extract.

197
00:10:48.648 --> 00:10:53.648
However, in the second go we noticed that
it extracted person, location and date.

198
00:10:54.353 --> 00:10:55.955
This is great.

199
00:10:55.955 --> 00:11:00.092
In this lab, you learned how to implement
pipelines that are able to loop,

200
00:11:00.092 --> 00:11:03.295
and in this case, you built a pipeline
